% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `time`, compiled by psi/espc.py
% into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: no part of `time` is
% printed or held.  It is MINIMAL: create/2 and set_count/2 only, for the
% alarm_watch stand-in's callers.  INTERPOLATED (labelled) from:
%   - pimfep##pimos_timer's local on_after/4 (held .ptf @10c):
%     `:create(#time,T), :set_count(T,N)` with N the timer's count, then
%     `:on_after(Watch,T)`;
%   - gog-kl1 ESP/PLAYSLOT.ESP:83-84 (ICOT Free Software): `:create(#time,
%     Time), :set_value(Time,0,0,S,M)` before `:on_after(Watch,Time)`;
%   - docs/simpos/required/classes.tsv (row `time`): create/2, now/2,
%     present/2, make_string/6, make_value/6; get_count/2, get_string/2,
%     get_value/5, minus/3, plus/3, set_count/2, set_value/5.  The scan
%     gained get_count/set_count/get_value/minus on 2026-11-25, when it
%     learned that `:now(#time,T)` returns an instance (gog-esp
%     CH_CLOCK.ESP:33-34 then :59-60 `:get_count(Obj!time,MS),
%     :set_count(Obj!time,MS+1000)`; the same lines in gog-kl1).
% Not stood in: set_value/5 and the rest.  Step 3k stands in now/2 and
% get_count/2 (labelled below), for the held pimos_timer get_count/3.
% The count is in MILLISECONDS: HELD-SOURCE gog-kl1 ESP/CH_CLOCK.ESP:60
% `:set_count(Obj!time,MS+1000),       % 1000 msec interval`.  PIMOS
% converts a timer count to msec before fep#on_at and fep#on_after
% (server/fep/timer/time_dvc.kl1:199-210, `time_unit_translator:
% trans({Unit,C},msec(C1))`).

class time has

% INTERPOLATED from: `:create(#time,Time)` (see above).
:create(Class, Time) :-
        :new(Class, Time);

% OURS (step 3k): the present count, read by now/2 below.
attribute clock := 0;

% :now(#time, T) -- T, a new time instance holding the present count.
% INTERPOLATED (step 3k) from: the held pimfep##pimos_timer get_count/3
% @86-8e (`:now(#time,T)`, then `:get_count(T,C)`, replied as `{Id, 1,
% C}`), and gog-esp CH_CLOCK.ESP:33-34 (`:now(#time,T)` answers an
% instance, above).  PIMOS reads the count as milliseconds
% (docs/fep_services.md §2.4, time_dvc.kl1:241-248).  There is no clock:
% the count is the class slot clock, 0 unless set (OURS).
:now(Class, Time) :-
        :new(Class, Time),
        Time!count := Class!clock;

instance

% INTERPOLATED: the representation (OURS).  The count is in
% MILLISECONDS (HELD-SOURCE: CH_CLOCK.ESP:60, above).
attribute count := 0;

% INTERPOLATED from: pimos_timer on_after/4 `:set_count(T,N)`.
:set_count(Time, Count) :-
        Time!count := Count;

% INTERPOLATED (step 3k) from: pimos_timer get_count/3 @8b-8e
% `:get_count(T,C)` and gog-esp CH_CLOCK.ESP:59 `:get_count(Obj!time,MS)`.
:get_count(Time, Count) :-
        Count = Time!count;

end.
